    introduction: `Forensic Ballistics is the science analyzing firearms, ammunition, bullet trajectories, and gunshot wound dynamics. Establishing firing distance (Contact vs Close vs Distant) and distinguishing entry from exit wounds are critical evidentiary tasks in homicidal and suicidal firearm investigations.`,
    whyThisMatters: `Tattooing (unburnt powder embedded in skin) is a true vital reaction proving close-range firing and cannot be washed off. Contact wounds over bone show stellate lacerated entry with muzzle imprints.`,
    simpleExplanation: `Forensic Ballistics studies guns and bullets. Firearms are Smoothbore (Shotguns firing pellets) or Rifled (Rifles/Pistols firing single bullets through spiral grooves). Spiral grooves (Lands & Grooves) impart spin to the bullet and leave unique Striation Marks (like fingerprints). Gunshot Range determined by entry wound signs: 1. Contact Wound (<1 cm): Muzzle imprint, stellate tear over bone, soot inside wound. 2. Close Range (<30-45 cm): Scorching (flame burn), Blackening (soot that washes off), and TATTOOING (unburnt powder granules embedded in skin that CANNOT wash off!). 3. Distant Range (>1 meter): Clean circular entry hole with Abrasion Collar and Grease Collar. Entry wounds are inverted; Exit wounds are everted, larger, and irregular.`,
